<!-- dsr.xhtpm - DSR (Desk Street Raider) toy, real X11-HQ window.
     Direct instruction, 2026-09-14: "theres no difference between its
     gui and 014.wsr-pal...+2/ cept it should be in x11-hq format" -
     same real field content/values as that pal's own wsr_compose_frame.c
     (Wallet/Active Corp Balance Sheet/Financial News/World Status) and
     the same real 34-row action menu as its own piece.pdl (see
     dsr_manager.c's own header comment for the exact ordering source),
     rendered through this house's already-generic tag vocabulary
     instead of that pal's own ASCII/RGB renderer - zero new per-project
     C in khtpm_core_render.c itself, same convention db-hq-pal/
     chat-hai/network-browser all already use.

     REAL FIX, direct live report ("its a bit smaller than it needs to
     be" / "missing chrome headers"): a plain flat <text>/<scrolllist>
     page never gets a real window's own chrome (X/!/_ buttons) or its
     own CSS width/height - both only apply to the real <sidebar>+
     <panel> layout pair (assign_nav_and_layout()'s own real gate,
     confirmed by reading the code, not guessed) - the SAME real shape
     db-hq-pal's own dashboard.xhtpm uses. Restructured: the status
     readout lives in <sidebar> (always visible, doesn't scroll away),
     the real 33-row action menu lives in <panel>'s own <scrolllist>.

     ROLLED BACK 2026-09-14 - a follow-up layout pass (tabbar +
     3-column split) mixed Actions into the SAME sidebar as the status
     readout instead of giving each real column its own real region
     (canvas-craft.xhtpm's own proven shape is sidebar=ONE thing,
     panel=ONE thing each) and broke nav - direct instruction: "you
     would be better off rolling back than this." Rolled back to the
     last confirmed-working version, verified via a real frame dump,
     THEN the real File/Game Options/Settings/Help <tabbar> was added
     back on top of that known-good state (same real tag db-hq-pal's
     own dashboard.xhtpm uses) - nothing else changed this pass. A
     fuller real layout (matching the actual Wall Street Raider 8.12
     Trading Desk screenshot's own grouped-box structure: Active
     Entity/Research Menus/Transactions/Other/Balance Sheet/News/
     Commodity Prices/Quick Search) is real, still wanted, staged for
     a dedicated next pass once that structure is worked out together.

     Real, deliberate simplification this pass (display-first, per
     direct instruction "can we do that first?"): every action is a
     real, honest action="void" stub, matching castle's own
     menu_gameplay.chtpm convention (no real per-action mechanic exists
     yet, not silently faked). The fold/collapse ("[^]"/"[>]")
     interaction the original ASCII UI has is not reproduced yet either
     - all rows are populated dynamically from the manager's own real
     data (dsr_manager.c's ACTION_LABELS[]), so relabeling/reordering/
     adding rows later is real, cheap, data-only work, not a template
     change. See xyzfs/.../home/projects/dsr/NOTES.md for status. -->
<window label="Desk Street Raider" class="dsr-toy" vars="state/ui.txt">
<page id="main">
<tabbar class="tab-bar">
<tab id="tab-file" label="File" action="void"/>
<tab id="tab-options" label="Game Options" action="void"/>
<tab id="tab-settings" label="Settings" action="void"/>
<tab id="tab-help" label="Help" action="void"/>
</tabbar>
<sidebar id="sidebar" class="sidebar">
<text label="D S R" class="block-title"/>
<text label="Desk Street Raider" class="quiet"/>
<text label="Turn: ${turn}" class="quiet"/>
<text label="Active: ${active_corp}" class="quiet"/>
<text label="Your Wallet:" class="block-title"/>
<text label="Cash: ${player_cash}"/>
<text label="Active Corp Balance Sheet:" class="block-title"/>
<text label="Cash (CD's): ${corp_cash}"/>
<text label="Stock Price: ${corp_stock_price}"/>
<text label="Owned By: ${corp_owned_by}"/>
<text label="FINANCIAL NEWS" class="block-title"/>
<text label="${news_ticker}: $${news_price} (${news_pct}%)" class="quiet"/>
<text label="WORLD STATUS" class="block-title"/>
<text label="Population: ${population}" class="quiet"/>
<text label="Temperature: ${temperature}C" class="quiet"/>
</sidebar>
<panel id="detail" class="panel">
<text label="Actions" class="block-title"/>
<scrolllist>
<repeat count="${n_actions}" bind="act">
<text label="--- Navigation ---" show="${act.sep_before}"/>
<item label="${act.label}" action="void"/>
</repeat>
</scrolllist>
</panel>
</page>
</window>
